# Rust and Tauri build output
/target
**/target

# Node
node_modules/
apps/*/dist
packages/*/dist

# `gen/` is NOT ignored wholesale: `tauri android init` / `tauri ios init` put the
# hand-editable Gradle and Xcode projects (manifests, signing, permissions) there,
# and those belong in the repo. Build output is ignored by the .gitignore files
# tauri generates inside gen/android and gen/apple; only the permission schemas,
# which tauri-build regenerates on every compile, are ignored here.
apps/native/src-tauri/gen/schemas

# Signing keys never belong in the repository, however they are named.
*.keystore
*.jks

# The Go reference builds its binary here (`make build` in reference/go).
reference/go/bin/

# Local state
.env
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
.DS_Store
.lean-ctx/

# The seeded Claude Design canvas payload (~2 MB, regenerated by gen.py + the
# design skill). The artboards themselves are *.dc.html and stay in the repo.
apps/native/design/*.html
!apps/native/design/*.dc.html
